    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0439" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-01-25T00:44:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-01-24T20:00:00+04:53"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 24, 1919, 12:44
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at] Omsk.</p>
                <p>“51. January 24, 8 p.m. Sir Charles
                        Eliot<anchor n="50" xml:id="d359-f1"/> has officially stated to
                    the Foreign Office here on behalf of his Government that, inasmuch as the Omsk
                    Government now represents the highest Russian power, Great Britain expresses its
                    warmest sympathy with Kolchak endeavors
                    to create a free Russian Government on the basis of public confidence as only
                    under such conditions can Russia return to its former place among the nations
                    and partake in the upbuilding of civilization.</p>
                <p>On January 21 Ambassador Regnault<anchor n="51" xml:id="d359-f2"/> handed
                        Kolchak a communication from the
                    French Government in which it expressed its pleasure at the union which has been
                    attained between the Denikin and
                        Kolchak governments. At the same
                    time the French Government <pb facs="0440" n="328" xml:id="pg328"/> expressed
                    satisfaction at the choice of Sazonoff as the common Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    of both. They point out way for the recognition of Admiral Kolchak. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
